{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The fat.</b> This is the fat of the entrails or the paunch." "<b>And the fat-tail.</b> From the kidneys downward, as is spelled out in Vayikra where it is stated (Leviticus 3), ״לְעֻמַּת הֶעָצֶה יְסִירֶנָּה״ — at the place where the kidneys meet (Ḥullin 11). And in the emurim of the bull the fat-tail is not mentioned, for the fat-tail is offered only with a lamb and a ewe and a ram, but an ox and a goat do not require a fat-tail." "<b>And the right thigh.</b> We find no burning of the right thigh with the emurim except this one alone." "<b>For it is a ram of consecration.</b> Whole — a term of wholeness, for it was made whole with everything. Scripture tells that the consecration-offerings are whole, for they make wholeness for the altar and for the one performing the service and for the owners; therefore I require the breast of it, to be his — the one performing the service — as a portion, and that is Mosheh who served in the consecrations; and the rest Aharon and his sons ate, for they are the owners, as spelled out in the matter."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:32.900289004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}